 612           * frequency deviates from the specified frequency.
 613           *
 614           * The frequency calibration is done as a one-time procedure.
 615           * Any desired test frequency within the normal range of the
 616           * Si5351 should be set, then the actual output frequency
 617           * should be measured as accurately as possible. The
 618           * difference between the measured and specified frequencies
 619           * should be calculated in Hertz, then multiplied by 10 in
 620           * order to get the parts-per-10 million value.
 621           *
 622           * Since the Si5351 itself has an intrinsic 0 PPM error, this
 623           * correction factor is good across the entire tuning range of
 624           * the Si5351. Once this calibration is done accurately, it
 625           * should not have to be done again for the same Si5351 and
 626           * crystal.
 627           */
